<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%- include('head'); -%>

  <body>
    <div class="wrap">
      <%- include('header'); -%>
        <h1>School Virtual Classroom & Meeting Space</h1>
        <section>
          <p>
            Welcome to the school's integrated peer-to-peer video conferencing module. You can use it right in your
            browser for virtual classes, tutoring, and collaborative study groups - no extra downloads required.
          </p>
          <p>
            Just share your session URL with students or colleagues and connect instantly.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <div id="roombox" class="flex">
            <span class="domain">school-portal/</span>
            <input type="text" placeholder="class-session-id" class="flex-1" />
            <button onClick="onJoin()">Start Session</button>
          </div>
          <div class="small light">Entering a session ID is optional - click "Start Session" to generate a random study
            room. Start the ID with "@" to make it an open campus room.</div>
          <br />
        </section>

        <section>
          <a href="/public" class="public-cta flex">
            <span class="flex-1">
              <strong>Find open campus rooms</strong>
              <div class="small light">Join public lectures, student clubs, or open study sessions.</div>
            </span>
            <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <h3>What is a virtual classroom session?</h3>
          <p>A session is a secure video chat space you access by visiting a unique link generated by the school portal.
            Just click the link, and you join the video call right away.</p>

          <h3>What is a private session?</h3>
          <p>All sessions are private by default. This means only students, parents, or staff you share the link with
            can find and join your room. This is ideal for one-on-one tutoring or parent-teacher conferences. To keep it
            strictly secure, generate a random name instead of a common word.</p>

          <h3>What is an open campus room?</h3>
          <p>Open rooms are sessions that start with "@" (e.g., @math-club). Any student or teacher can discover these
            rooms by visiting the <a href="/public">Open Campus Directory</a> and join them. It's a great way to host
            public Q&A sessions or school-wide study groups.</p>

          <h3>Is there a maximum number of participants?</h3>
          <p>Yes. Currently, a maximum of 4 people can be in a collaborative room at the same time.</p>

          <h3>Why is there a 4-person limit?</h3>
          <p>This module connects users directly to each other (peer-to-peer) to ensure high privacy without overloading
            school servers. With 4 people, your device seamlessly handles the video streams, making it perfect for small
            group projects, specialized tutoring, and focused discussions.</p>

          <div class="spacer"></div>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <script type="text/javascript">
          const inputElement = document.querySelector("#roombox input");

          const onJoin = () =>
            window.location.pathname = inputElement.value || "random";

          inputElement.addEventListener("keypress", (e) => {
            if (e.key === "Enter") {
              e.preventDefault();
              onJoin();
            }
          });
        </script>

        <%- include('footer'); -%>
    </div>
  </body>

</html>